      "content": "It is evident that the indigenous societies lack the necessary institutional framework and rational understanding to manage complex modern governance effectively. Their social structures, while rich in custom, often lack the uniformity required for efficient commerce or stable public health administration. We arrive not to dominate, but to provide the necessary scaffolding—order, codified law, and technological expertise—that their own customs have failed to develop. This stewardship is therefore a natural progression, akin to a capable parent guiding a less mature child towards full adulthood.",
